%% HTTP prefix: /api/v1. API lane includes verified middleware and errorHandler.
%% Grouped read and validation calls short-circuit on error. No Repository layer is implied.
%% Payment remains SUCCESS until actual refund confirmation, see REC-05.
sequenceDiagram
    actor A as Receptionist
    participant UI as CancelSubscription
    participant API as Express middleware / errorHandler
    participant C as subsController
    participant S as subscriptionsService
    participant DB as Prisma / PostgreSQL

    A->>UI: Confirm cancellation of paid ACTIVE or SCHEDULED membership
    UI->>API: PATCH /api/v1/subscriptions/:id/status (CANCELLED)
    activate API
    API->>API: authenticate, checkFacilityScope, authorize(RECEPTIONIST), validate request
    alt request guard rejects
        API-->>UI: 400 / 401 / 403 error
    else request accepted
        API->>C: updateSubscriptionStatus(req, res, next)
        activate C
        C->>S: updateSubscriptionStatus(id, CANCELLED)
        activate S
        S->>DB: Read subscription, original collected payment and cancellation context
        activate DB
        DB-->>S: Requested records and validation context
        deactivate DB
        S->>S: SCHEDULED refund is 100 percent, ACTIVE staff refund is prorated from original sold duration and capped at collected amount
        S->>S: Reject FREE and invalid state transitions, manual SUSPENDED is forbidden
        alt subscription missing or cancellation state invalid
            S-->>C: 400 / 404 / 409
        else business conditions satisfied
            S->>DB: Locked transaction CAS CANCELLED, revoke source bookings and record refund request if amount positive
            activate DB
            DB-->>S: Saved result
            deactivate DB
            S-->>C: Cancelled subscription and requested refund amount
        end
        deactivate S
        C-->>API: response or next(error)
        deactivate C
        API-->>UI: 200 result or mapped error
    end
    deactivate API
    UI-->>A: Show result or actionable error

